---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Ref from '../components/Ref.astro';

const upgrade = [
  'An original outfit for Makoto Daito',
  'A set of 4 weapons',
  'A set of 4 Skilled Performers, for the show business side of the game',
  'A set of 3 Stage Production Items',
  'A Special Promotional Poster',
  'A Record Player that plays the soundtrack in game',
  'An Electronic Camera',
];
const rows = [
  { label: 'Format', values: ['Digital and physical', 'Digital', 'Physical only'] },
  { label: 'Platforms', values: ['PS5, Xbox Series X|S, PC', 'PS5, Xbox Series X|S, PC', 'PS5 and Xbox Series X|S'] },
  { label: 'US price', values: ['$69.99', '$89.99', '$129.99'] },
  { label: 'The game', values: [true, true, true] },
  { label: 'Pre-order weapon, if you pre-order', values: [true, true, true] },
  { label: 'Deluxe Upgrade items', values: [false, true, 'As a download code'] },
  { label: 'SteelBook case', values: [false, false, true] },
  { label: '12-inch vinyl record', values: [false, false, true] },
  { label: "Collector's box", values: [false, false, true] },
];
---

<Base
  title="Stranger Than Heaven Editions Compared: Standard vs Deluxe"
  description="Stranger Than Heaven Standard, Deluxe and Collector's editions side by side: prices, Deluxe Upgrade contents, and how the pre-order weapon works."
  path="/editions/"
>
  <h1>Editions compared</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Three editions: Standard at $69.99, Deluxe at $89.99 and a physical Collector's Edition at $129.99. Every one of
    them includes the same game.
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Standard</th><th scope="col">Deluxe</th><th scope="col">Collector's</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{row.label}</th>
            {row.values.map((value) => (
              <td>{value === true ? <span class="yes">Yes</span> : value === false ? <span class="no">No</span> : value}</td>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">
    Prices are US store prices <Ref ids={['steam', 'rpgsite', 'gamestop']} />. Contents are from SEGA's announcement
    and the US store listings <Ref ids={['sega-0608', 'rpgsite']} />. Checked 17 November 2026.
  </p>

  <h2>What the Deluxe Upgrade adds</h2>
  <ul class="prose">
    {upgrade.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
  </ul>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      All seven are in-game items. None is described as extra story. SEGA also says the Deluxe Upgrade can be bought
      on its own at any time by anyone who owns the Standard Edition <Ref ids="sega-0608" />, so starting with
      Standard and upgrading later is an option. Its separate price has not been announced.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The pre-order bonus</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Pre-ordering a copy, digital or physical, comes with one weapon: Dosu: Kagekiri. The Collector's Edition
      carries it as a download code. SEGA's small print matters here <Ref ids="sega-0608" />:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>It is not in your hands from the first minute. It unlocks as you advance through the game.</li>
      <li>You need the latest update installed to use it.</li>
      <li>SEGA advises confirming that the bonus is available where you pre-order, so check the listing first.</li>
      <li>SEGA says the contents and timing of the bonus can change without notice.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>The Collector's Edition</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      A boxed edition with a physical copy of the game, a SteelBook case, a 12-inch vinyl record that includes the
      main theme, a collector's box, and download codes for the Deluxe Upgrade and the pre-order weapon. In the US it
      is listed at $129.99 for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X <Ref ids="gamestop" />. SEGA says supplies are limited
      <Ref ids="sega-0608" />.
    </p>
    <p>
      In Japan the boxed edition is for PS5 and costs 18,000 yen. The standard physical edition is 9,900 yen and the
      standard download 8,990 yen. All three prices include tax <Ref ids="sega-0608" />.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Which one?</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You just want to play:</strong> Standard, or Game Pass if you have it.</li>
      <li><strong>You want the extras but are not sure:</strong> Standard now. The upgrade is sold separately.</li>
      <li><strong>You know you want everything digital:</strong> Deluxe.</li>
      <li><strong>You want the record and the SteelBook:</strong> Collector's, and do not wait, since stock is limited.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Shops sometimes add extras of their own. Prima Games reported a poster with Amazon pre-orders
      <Ref ids="prima" />. Offers like that vary by country and can end early, so check the listing itself.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
